**Evaluating page item movement**

I'm thinking about how to adjust the positions of page items after toggling some settings. I want to compute the delta based on the change in the page's bounds from old to new. If the page shifts from a left position of -w to 0, then all the items need to move accordingly to maintain their relative positions. I definitely need to keep track of the old page bounds because after the toggle, it's unclear if items have moved or stayed in place.**Examining script functions**

I’m working through how the script manages margins, master pages, and positioning. It seems like it handles applying margins and page references, with some additional steps for creating side-specific single-page masters. I need to focus on duplicating items from the old master page to the new one and ensuring the geometric bounds are set correctly. There’s a function at play that might create masters in a non-facing layout after the switch, which I need to clarify.
[/Thinking]

Below is an optimized Adobe InDesign ExtendScript (`.jsx`) that converts a **facing-pages / spreads document** into a **single-page document**, while preserving:

- Page size
- Page margins
- Page item positions relative to their original page
- Applied master-page logic
- Left/right master-page appearance by creating side-specific one-page masters

> **Important:** Run this on a copy of your document first. The script is designed to preserve layout, but complex documents with overridden/anchored/master-dependent objects should always be checked visually afterward.

---

## InDesign JSX Script

Save as something like:

```text
Convert_Spreads_To_Single_Pages.jsx
```

Then run from InDesign via:

```text
Window > Utilities > Scripts
```

```jsx
/*
    Convert Spreads / Facing Pages Document to Single Page Document
    --------------------------------------------------------------

    What this script does:
    - Converts the active document from facing pages to single pages.
    - Preserves page item positions relative to their original page.
    - Preserves page margins.
    - Preserves applied master appearance by creating one-page master spreads
      based on the original left/right master pages.
    - Reapplies the appropriate new one-page master to each document page.

    Recommended:
    - Run on a duplicate/copy of your document.
*/

(function () {
    if (app.documents.length === 0) {
        alert("No document is open.");
        return;
    }

    var doc = app.activeDocument;

    app.doScript(
        function () {
            main(doc);
        },
        ScriptLanguage.JAVASCRIPT,
        undefined,
        UndoModes.ENTIRE_SCRIPT,
        "Convert Spreads to Single Pages"
    );

    function main(doc) {
        var oldRulerOrigin = doc.viewPreferences.rulerOrigin;
        doc.viewPreferences.rulerOrigin = RulerOrigin.PAGE_ORIGIN;

        var oldFacing = doc.documentPreferences.facingPages;

        if (!oldFacing) {
            alert("This document is already a single-page / non-facing-pages document.");
            doc.viewPreferences.rulerOrigin = oldRulerOrigin;
            return;
        }

        // Prevent page shuffling from altering page order.
        doc.documentPreferences.allowPageShuffle = false;

        for (var s = 0; s < doc.spreads.length; s++) {
            doc.spreads[s].allowPageShuffle = false;
        }

        // Store layer lock states and unlock temporarily.
        var layerStates = unlockLayers(doc);

        // Capture document page data before conversion.
        var pageData = captureDocumentPages(doc);

        // Capture original master page data before conversion.
        var masterData = captureMasterPages(doc);

        // Convert to single pages.
        doc.documentPreferences.facingPages = false;

        // Force redraw/recompose.
        app.activeWindow.activePage = doc.pages[0];
        doc.recompose();

        // Create side-specific one-page masters from original master pages.
        var masterMap = createSinglePageMasters(doc, masterData);

        // Restore page margins, applied masters, and page item positions.
        restoreDocumentPages(doc, pageData, masterMap);

        // Restore layer locks.
        restoreLayers(layerStates);

        doc.viewPreferences.rulerOrigin = oldRulerOrigin;

        alert("Done. The document has been converted to single pages.");
    }

    /*
        Capture document page info:
        - page id
        - page bounds
        - margin preferences
        - applied master
        - original side
        - page items with positions relative to the page
    */
    function captureDocumentPages(doc) {
        var data = [];

        for (var i = 0; i < doc.pages.length; i++) {
            var p = doc.pages[i];

            var pb = p.bounds;
            var pageTop = pb[0];
            var pageLeft = pb[1];

            var itemData = [];
            var items = p.pageItems;

            for (var j = 0; j < items.length; j++) {
                var it = items[j];

                if (!isValidPageItem(it)) {
                    continue;
                }

                unlockItemTree(it);

                try {
                    var gb = it.geometricBounds;

                    itemData.push({
                        id: it.id,
                        relBounds: [
                            gb[0] - pageTop,
                            gb[1] - pageLeft,
                            gb[2] - pageTop,
                            gb[3] - pageLeft
                        ]
                    });
                } catch (e) {
                    // Ignore non-positionable items.
                }
            }

            data.push({
                id: p.id,
                name: p.name,
                side: String(p.side),
                bounds: [
                    p.bounds[0],
                    p.bounds[1],
                    p.bounds[2],
                    p.bounds[3]
                ],
                appliedMasterName: p.appliedMaster ? p.appliedMaster.name : null,
                appliedMasterId: p.appliedMaster ? p.appliedMaster.id : null,
                margins: getMargins(p),
                items: itemData
            });
        }

        return data;
    }

    /*
        Capture original master page side data.
        This is necessary because a left master page and a right master page
        may have different objects and margins.
    */
    function captureMasterPages(doc) {
        var result = [];

        for (var m = 0; m < doc.masterSpreads.length; m++) {
            var ms = doc.masterSpreads[m];

            for (var p = 0; p < ms.pages.length; p++) {
                var mp = ms.pages[p];

                var pb = mp.bounds;
                var pageTop = pb[0];
                var pageLeft = pb[1];

                var itemData = [];
                var items = mp.pageItems;

                for (var i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {
                    var it = items[i];

                    if (!isValidPageItem(it)) {
                        continue;
                    }

                    unlockItemTree(it);

                    try {
                        var gb = it.geometricBounds;

                        itemData.push({
                            ref: it,
                            relBounds: [
                                gb[0] - pageTop,
                                gb[1] - pageLeft,
                                gb[2] - pageTop,
                                gb[3] - pageLeft
                            ]
                        });
                    } catch (e) {
                        // Ignore non-positionable items.
                    }
                }

                result.push({
                    masterName: ms.name,
                    masterId: ms.id,
                    pageIndex: p,
                    side: String(mp.side),
                    margins: getMargins(mp),
                    items: itemData
                });
            }
        }

        return result;
    }

    /*
        Create a one-page master for each original master-page side.
        Example:
        Original master: A-Master with left and right pages
        New masters:
        - A-Master_LEFT
        - A-Master_RIGHT
    */
    function createSinglePageMasters(doc, masterData) {
        var map = {};

        for (var i = 0; i < masterData.length; i++) {
            var md = masterData[i];

            var key = md.masterId + "|" + md.side;

            if (map[key]) {
                continue;
            }

            var newMaster = doc.masterSpreads.add();

            try {
                newMaster.name = makeUniqueMasterName(doc, md.masterName + "_" + sideSuffix(md.side));
            } catch (e) {
                // Ignore naming issues.
            }

            // Ensure master is one page.
            while (newMaster.pages.length > 1) {
                newMaster.pages[-1].remove();
            }

            var newPage = newMaster.pages[0];

            setMargins(newPage, md.margins);

            var npb = newPage.bounds;
            var newTop = npb[0];
            var newLeft = npb[1];

            // Duplicate original master items to the new one-page master.
            for (var j = 0; j < md.items.length; j++) {
                var srcInfo = md.items[j];

                try {
                    if (!srcInfo.ref.isValid) {
                        continue;
                    }

                    var dup = srcInfo.ref.duplicate(newPage);

                    try {
                        dup.geometricBounds = [
                            newTop + srcInfo.relBounds[0],
                            newLeft + srcInfo.relBounds[1],
                            newTop + srcInfo.relBounds[2],
                            newLeft + srcInfo.relBounds[3]
                        ];
                    } catch (gbErr) {
                        // Some objects may not allow direct geometricBounds setting.
                        // Fall back to moving by delta if possible.
                        try {
                            var gb = dup.geometricBounds;
                            var targetTop = newTop + srcInfo.relBounds[0];
                            var targetLeft = newLeft + srcInfo.relBounds[1];
                            dup.move(undefined, [targetLeft - gb[1], targetTop - gb[0]]);
                        } catch (moveErr) {}
                    }
                } catch (e) {
                    // Ignore items that cannot be duplicated.
                }
            }

            map[key] = newMaster;
        }

        return map;
    }

    /*
        Restore page data after facingPages has been disabled.
    */
    function restoreDocumentPages(doc, pageData, masterMap) {
        for (var i = 0; i < pageData.length; i++) {
            var pd = pageData[i];
            var p = getPageById(doc, pd.id);

            if (!p) {
                continue;
            }

            setMargins(p, pd.margins);

            // Reapply equivalent one-page master if original had one.
            if (pd.appliedMasterId !== null) {
                var key = pd.appliedMasterId + "|" + pd.side;

                if (masterMap[key]) {
                    try {
                        p.appliedMaster = masterMap[key];
                    } catch (e) {}
                }
            } else {
                try {
                    p.appliedMaster = NothingEnum.NOTHING;
                } catch (e) {}
            }

            // Restore page item positions relative to the new single page.
            var pb = p.bounds;
            var pageTop = pb[0];
            var pageLeft = pb[1];

            for (var j = 0; j < pd.items.length; j++) {
                var itemInfo = pd.items[j];
                var it = getPageItemById(doc, itemInfo.id);

                if (!it) {
                    continue;
                }

                unlockItemTree(it);

                try {
                    it.geometricBounds = [
                        pageTop + itemInfo.relBounds[0],
                        pageLeft + itemInfo.relBounds[1],
                        pageTop + itemInfo.relBounds[2],
                        pageLeft + itemInfo.relBounds[3]
                    ];
                } catch (gbErr) {
                    // Fallback move method.
                    try {
                        var gb = it.geometricBounds;
                        var targetTop = pageTop + itemInfo.relBounds[0];
                        var targetLeft = pageLeft + itemInfo.relBounds[1];
                        it.move(undefined, [targetLeft - gb[1], targetTop - gb[0]]);
                    } catch (moveErr) {}
                }
            }
        }
    }

    function getMargins(pageOrMasterPage) {
        var m = pageOrMasterPage.marginPreferences;

        return {
            top: m.top,
            bottom: m.bottom,
            left: m.left,
            right: m.right,
            columnCount: m.columnCount,
            columnGutter: m.columnGutter
        };
    }

    function setMargins(pageOrMasterPage, data) {
        var m = pageOrMasterPage.marginPreferences;

        try { m.top = data.top; } catch (e) {}
        try { m.bottom = data.bottom; } catch (e) {}
        try { m.left = data.left; } catch (e) {}
        try { m.right = data.right; } catch (e) {}
        try { m.columnCount = data.columnCount; } catch (e) {}
        try { m.columnGutter = data.columnGutter; } catch (e) {}
    }

    function getPageById(doc, id) {
        for (var i = 0; i < doc.pages.length; i++) {
            if (doc.pages[i].id === id) {
                return doc.pages[i];
            }
        }

        return null;
    }

    function getPageItemById(doc, id) {
        try {
            return doc.pageItems.itemByID(id);
        } catch (e) {
            return null;
        }
    }

    function isValidPageItem(it) {
        if (!it) {
            return false;
        }

        try {
            if (!it.isValid) {
                return false;
            }
        } catch (e) {
            return false;
        }

        return true;
    }

    function unlockLayers(doc) {
        var states = [];

        for (var i = 0; i < doc.layers.length; i++) {
            var l = doc.layers[i];

            states.push({
                layer: l,
                locked: l.locked,
                visible: l.visible
            });

            try { l.locked = false; } catch (e) {}
            try { l.visible = true; } catch (e) {}
        }

        return states;
    }

    function restoreLayers(states) {
        for (var i = 0; i < states.length; i++) {
            try { states[i].layer.locked = states[i].locked; } catch (e) {}
            try { states[i].layer.visible = states[i].visible; } catch (e) {}
        }
    }

    function unlockItemTree(item) {
        try { item.locked = false; } catch (e) {}

        try {
            if (item.allPageItems && item.allPageItems.length) {
                for (var i = 0; i < item.allPageItems.length; i++) {
                    try { item.allPageItems[i].locked = false; } catch (e) {}
                }
            }
        } catch (e) {}
    }

    function sideSuffix(sideString) {
        sideString = String(sideString).toLowerCase();

        if (sideString.indexOf("left") !== -1) {
            return "LEFT";
        }

        if (sideString.indexOf("right") !== -1) {
            return "RIGHT";
        }

        return "SINGLE";
    }

    function makeUniqueMasterName(doc, baseName) {
        var name = baseName;
        var counter = 1;

        while (masterNameExists(doc, name)) {
            name = baseName + "_" + counter;
            counter++;
        }

        return name;
    }

    function masterNameExists(doc, name) {
        for (var i = 0; i < doc.masterSpreads.length; i++) {
            if (doc.masterSpreads[i].name === name) {
                return true;
            }
        }

        return false;
    }

})();
```

---

## Notes

This script converts master-page usage like this:

```text
A-Master, left page  -> A-Master_LEFT
A-Master, right page -> A-Master_RIGHT
B-Master, left page  -> B-Master_LEFT
B-Master, right page -> B-Master_RIGHT
```

This is the safest way to preserve the appearance of layouts that depend on different left/right master-page content.

The original master spreads remain in the document. The new single-page masters are applied to the converted document pages.

This is intentional, because a non-facing-pages document cannot always faithfully use the left/right side of a facing-page master in the same way as the original spread-based document.

