## Notes

This script converts master-page usage like this:

```text
A-Master, left page  -> A-Master_LEFT
A-Master, right page -> A-Master_RIGHT
B-Master, left page  -> B-Master_LEFT
B-Master, right page -> B-Master_RIGHT
```

This is the safest way to preserve the appearance of layouts that depend on different left/right master-page content.

The original master spreads remain in the document. The new single-page masters are applied to the converted document pages.

This is intentional, because a non-facing-pages document cannot always faithfully use the left/right side of a facing-page master in the same way as the original spread-based document.
